# Stop Backend after changes

After editing Backend code (or before `dotnet build` / `dotnet run` / `dotnet test` that rebuilds Backend), stop any running Backend process so `Backend.exe` is not locked (MSB3027 / MSB3021).

```powershell
Get-Process -Name Backend -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Stop-Process -Force
```

Do this at the end of the change set, not mid-edit unless a rebuild is required immediately.
